<%#
    Consent, the Google tag, and attribution capture, shared by every
    OneUptime-owned origin that measures anything: the marketing site, the docs,
    the API reference, sign-up and the dashboard.

    It is one file rather than a copy per origin because the storage contract
    has to stay byte-identical: the same 'cookiesAccepted' values, the same
    'clickIds' and 'firstTouch' JSON shapes. Several copies is how those stop
    agreeing - and these origins share one hostname on OneUptime Cloud, so an
    answer given on the marketing site has to be the answer the product honours.

    Locals:
      enableGoogleTagManager  OneUptime's own measurement is on (the hosted
                              product). False on self-hosted installs, which
                              load no Google tag at all.
      googleTagMode           'tag-manager' (default) loads the Google Tag
                              Manager container with all of its tags.
                              'analytics-only' loads Google Analytics and
                              nothing else - for sign-up and the dashboard,
                              where advertising pixels and visitor
                              identification tools have no business running.

    Status pages and public dashboards must NOT include this: they belong to
    OneUptime's customers, and their visitors are not OneUptime's to measure.

    Include it in <head>, before anything that reads the consent state. Home
    resolves it as ../../Common/Server/Views/Partials/AnalyticsConsent and the
    App FeatureSets as ../../../../Common/Server/Views/Partials/... (one more
    ../ from a Partials folder); /usr/src/Common is present in both images.

    Deliberately NOT here: the marketing site's PostHog loader (its project
    key is Home's) and its home/-prefixed events. Home asks
    window.oneUptimeConsent.whenAllowed to run them. Reporting on a captured
    touch is handed back to the page through
    window.oneUptimeOnAttributionCaptured for the same reason.
-%>
<% const tagsEnabled = typeof enableGoogleTagManager !== 'undefined' ? enableGoogleTagManager : false; %>
<% const tagMode = (typeof googleTagMode !== 'undefined' && googleTagMode === 'analytics-only') ? 'analytics-only' : 'tag-manager'; %>
<!--
    Consent.

    Nothing that measures you runs until it is allowed. Where the law asks for
    consent first (the EEA, the UK and Switzerland), that means until you press
    "Accept all". Elsewhere measurement runs until you press "Reject all", and
    a refusal stops it, clears what it stored and is remembered. A browser
    sending Global Privacy Control counts as a refusal unless you accept.
-->
<% if (tagsEnabled) { %>
<!--
    The dataLayer and the gtag shim, defined before both the consent signals
    below and the tag itself.

    Deliberately inside the enableGoogleTagManager gate. A self-hosted install
    loads no Google tag at all, and every OneUptime event guards on
    `typeof dataLayer !== 'undefined'` - so creating the array there would turn
    those no-ops into an array that grows for the life of the page and that
    nothing will ever read.
-->
<script>
    window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
    function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }
</script>
<% } %>

<script>
    window.oneUptimeConsent = (function () {
        var STORAGE_KEY = 'cookiesAccepted';

        /*
         * Time zones of the places whose law asks for consent before anything
         * non-essential is stored: the EEA (with the EU's outermost regions,
         * and Cyprus, whose zone is filed under Asia), the UK and Switzerland.
         *
         * Over-inclusive on purpose. Every Europe/ zone matches, including
         * countries outside the EEA; being asked first there costs a click,
         * while not asking where the law requires it is the defect this fixes.
         */
        var CONSENT_FIRST_TIME_ZONE = /^(Europe\/|Atlantic\/(Azores|Canary|Faroe|Faeroe|Madeira|Reykjavik)$|Africa\/Ceuta$|Arctic\/Longyearbyen$|Asia\/(Nicosia|Famagusta)$|America\/(Cayenne|Guadeloupe|Martinique|Marigot|St_Barthelemy)$|Indian\/(Mayotte|Reunion)$)/;

        // What privacy-hardened browsers report instead of the real zone.
        var HIDDEN_TIME_ZONE = /^(Etc\/|UTC$|GMT$|Universal$|Zulu$)/;

        /*
         * First-party cookies set by the tags behind the banner: Google
         * Analytics and Ads, Meta, Microsoft Advertising, Reddit and X.
         */
        var MEASUREMENT_COOKIE = /^(_ga|_gid|_gat|_gcl_|_fbp|_fbc|_uet|_rdt_|_twclid)/;

        // PostHog keeps its state in a cookie and in localStorage, both ph_*.
        var ANALYTICS_STORAGE = /^ph_/;

        var allowedCallbacks = [];
        var changeListeners = [];

        /*
         * The answer given on this page, kept in memory too: a browser that
         * refuses storage (private modes, blocked site data) would otherwise
         * forget it the moment anything asked again.
         */
        var pageAnswer = null;

        function readRaw() {
            try {
                return window.localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
            } catch (e) {
                /*
                 * Private mode, disabled storage, or a cross-origin sandbox.
                 * Unreadable storage is not consent.
                 */
                return null;
            }
        }

        function state() {
            if (pageAnswer) { return pageAnswer; }

            var raw = readRaw();
            if (raw === 'true') { return 'granted'; }
            if (raw === 'false') { return 'denied'; }
            return 'unset';
        }

        function isGranted() {
            return state() === 'granted';
        }

        function timeZone() {
            try {
                return Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone || '';
            } catch (e) {
                return '';
            }
        }

        /*
         * Whether this visitor has to say yes before anything non-essential
         * runs, decided from the browser's time zone. A zone that is missing
         * or hidden asks first: when we cannot tell, we do not assume.
         */
        function requiresConsentFirst() {
            var zone = timeZone();

            if (!zone || HIDDEN_TIME_ZONE.test(zone)) {
                return true;
            }

            return CONSENT_FIRST_TIME_ZONE.test(zone);
        }

        /*
         * Global Privacy Control: a standing "no" from the browser. The
         * Cookie Policy says it is honoured; this is where. Pressing "Accept
         * all" overrides it, since that is the more specific answer.
         */
        function hasGlobalPrivacyControl() {
            try {
                return Boolean(window.navigator && window.navigator.globalPrivacyControl === true);
            } catch (e) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        /*
         * The one rule every measuring tag on the page follows. An answer on
         * the banner always wins; with no answer, Global Privacy Control means
         * no, and otherwise it depends on where the visitor is.
         */
        function isAllowed() {
            var current = state();

            if (current === 'granted') { return true; }
            if (current === 'denied') { return false; }
            if (hasGlobalPrivacyControl()) { return false; }

            return !requiresConsentFirst();
        }

        /*
         * Consent Mode v2. The defaults go out before the tag loads, granted
         * only when measurement is allowed, and every answer is sent as an
         * update - so a refusal reaches Google tags already on the page.
         */
        function pushConsentSignal(mode, granted) {
            /*
             * No tag, nothing to tell. On a self-hosted install gtag is never
             * defined; the banner's answer is still recorded either way.
             */
            if (typeof window.gtag !== 'function') {
                return;
            }

            var value = granted ? 'granted' : 'denied';
            var signal = {
                ad_storage: value,
                ad_user_data: value,
                ad_personalization: value,
                analytics_storage: value,
                functionality_storage: value,
                personalization_storage: value,
                security_storage: 'granted'
            };

            if (mode === 'default') {
                signal.wait_for_update = 500;
            }

            window.gtag('consent', mode, signal);
        }

        function cookieNames() {
            try {
                return (document.cookie ? document.cookie.split(';') : []).map(function (cookie) {
                    return cookie.split('=')[0].trim();
                });
            } catch (e) {
                return [];
            }
        }

        /*
         * Tags set their cookies on the registrable domain (.oneuptime.com)
         * as well as the host, so each is expired on every parent domain up to
         * that one. A browser ignores the write for a domain the cookie is not
         * on, which costs nothing.
         */
        function expireCookie(name) {
            var labels = String((window.location && window.location.hostname) || '').split('.');
            var domains = [''];

            for (var i = 0; i < labels.length - 1; i++) {
                domains.push('.' + labels.slice(i).join('.'));
            }

            domains.forEach(function (domain) {
                try {
                    document.cookie = name + '=; expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT; path=/' + (domain ? '; domain=' + domain : '');
                } catch (e) {
                    // Cookies unavailable; nothing to expire.
                }
            });
        }

        function clearMeasurementCookies() {
            cookieNames().forEach(function (name) {
                if (MEASUREMENT_COOKIE.test(name)) {
                    expireCookie(name);
                }
            });
        }

        function clearAnalyticsStorage() {
            cookieNames().forEach(function (name) {
                if (ANALYTICS_STORAGE.test(name)) {
                    expireCookie(name);
                }
            });

            try {
                var keys = [];
                for (var i = 0; i < window.localStorage.length; i++) {
                    keys.push(window.localStorage.key(i));
                }
                keys.forEach(function (key) {
                    if (key && ANALYTICS_STORAGE.test(key)) {
                        window.localStorage.removeItem(key);
                    }
                });
            } catch (e) {
                // Storage unavailable; there is nothing in it to clear.
            }
        }

        function notify(allowed) {
            changeListeners.forEach(function (listener) {
                try {
                    listener(allowed);
                } catch (e) {
                    // One broken listener must not stop the others hearing.
                }
            });

            if (allowed) {
                allowedCallbacks.splice(0, allowedCallbacks.length).forEach(function (callback) {
                    try {
                        callback();
                    } catch (e) {
                        // One broken tag must not stop the others loading.
                    }
                });
            }
        }

        function set(granted) {
            pageAnswer = granted ? 'granted' : 'denied';

            try {
                window.localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, granted ? 'true' : 'false');
            } catch (e) {
                // Nothing to persist to. The answer still holds on this page.
            }

            pushConsentSignal('update', granted);

            if (!granted) {
                clearMeasurementCookies();
                clearAnalyticsStorage();
            }

            notify(granted);
        }

        /*
         * Runs callback once measurement is allowed: now, if it already is, or
         * the moment the visitor accepts. Tags load through this, so nothing
         * measuring starts on a page where it is not allowed.
         */
        function whenAllowed(callback) {
            if (isAllowed()) {
                callback();
                return;
            }

            allowedCallbacks.push(callback);
        }

        // Told true or false every time the visitor answers.
        function onChange(listener) {
            changeListeners.push(listener);
        }

        pushConsentSignal('default', isAllowed());

        /*
         * Not allowed means nothing left behind from an earlier visit either:
         * the tags ran unconditionally until this file gated them.
         */
        if (!isAllowed()) {
            clearMeasurementCookies();
        }

        return {
            state: state,
            isGranted: isGranted,
            isAllowed: isAllowed,
            requiresConsentFirst: requiresConsentFirst,
            whenAllowed: whenAllowed,
            onChange: onChange,
            grant: function () { set(true); },
            deny: function () { set(false); }
        };
    })();
</script>
<% if (tagsEnabled) { %>

<!--
    The Google tag, loaded only once measurement is allowed.
<% if (tagMode === 'analytics-only') { %>
    Google Analytics alone, sent the product's key events by
    Common/Utils/Analytics.ts. No container, so no advertising pixel or
    visitor identification tool can run here, whatever the container holds.
<% } else { %>
    The Google Tag Manager container, with every tag it holds.
<% } %>
-->
<script>
    (function () {
        var loaded = false;

        window.oneUptimeGoogleTagMode = '<%= tagMode %>';

        function loadGoogleTag() {
            if (loaded) {
                return;
            }

            /*
             * Not while a single-use bearer token is still in the address bar.
             * See Common/Server/Views/Partials/SensitiveUrlToken.ejs: the
             * bootstrap normally removes the token before this runs, and this
             * guard only fires when it could not - the tag would otherwise
             * send the URL, token and all, with its first hit.
             */
            if (window.__ONEUPTIME_SENSITIVE_URL_TOKEN_PENDING__) {
                return;
            }

            loaded = true;

            var script = document.createElement('script');
            script.async = true;
<% if (tagMode === 'analytics-only') { %>
            script.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-76XZF1WF3Z';
            window.gtag('js', new Date());
            window.gtag('config', 'G-76XZF1WF3Z');
<% } else { %>
            window.dataLayer.push({ 'gtm.start': new Date().getTime(), event: 'gtm.js' });
            script.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id=GTM-PKQD5WH';
<% } %>

            var firstScript = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];
            if (firstScript && firstScript.parentNode) {
                firstScript.parentNode.insertBefore(script, firstScript);
            } else {
                document.head.appendChild(script);
            }
        }

        window.oneUptimeConsent.whenAllowed(loadGoogleTag);
    })();
</script>
<% } %>

<!--
    Attribution capture (UTM parameters + ad platform click IDs), and the
    reader that hands it on to the signup form (through localStorage, same
    origin).

    STORAGE MODEL

    - Last-touch UTM values live in the individual utm* localStorage keys, read
      by the signup page and stored on the User record.
    - Last-touch click IDs live as a JSON object under 'clickIds'.
    - The visitor's first attributed visit is preserved as JSON under
      'firstTouch' and never overwritten.

    A visit counts as a new "touch" if it carries ANY utm parameter or ad click
    ID - Google Ads auto-tagging sends only gclid, no UTMs.

    CONSENT

    A touch is stored only while measurement is allowed. A visitor who has not
    been asked yet keeps this page's touch in memory, and it is stored the
    moment they accept; a refusal clears everything stored, and nothing is
    read back or handed to Cal.com while measurement is not allowed.

    CAL.COM BOOKINGS

    window.oneUptimeCalAttributionMetadata(bookingKind) flattens the same
    attribution into the scalar string map Cal.com accepts as booking metadata.
    Cal hands it back on its BOOKING_CREATED webhook, which is delivered to the
    CRM - not to OneUptime, which receives no booking webhook at all
    (Docs/analytics/enterprise-conversion-tracking.md).
-->
<script>
    (function () {
        /*
         * Must stay in step with UtmWireKeyToPropertyKey in
         * Common/Types/Marketing/Attribution.ts - the signup door whitelists on
         * that map, so a key written here that is missing there is silently
         * dropped on arrival. AttributionCapture.test.ts asserts the two are
         * identical.
         */
        var UTM_KEY_MAP = {
            'utm_source': 'utmSource',
            'utm_medium': 'utmMedium',
            'utm_campaign': 'utmCampaign',
            'utm_term': 'utmTerm',
            'utm_content': 'utmContent',
            'utm_id': 'utmId',
            'utm_source_platform': 'utmSourcePlatform',
            'utm_creative_format': 'utmCreativeFormat',
            'utm_marketing_tactic': 'utmMarketingTactic'
        };

        /*
         * Must stay in step with AdClickIdKeys in
         * Common/Types/Marketing/Attribution.ts - the server whitelists on that
         * list, so a key sent from here that is missing there is silently
         * dropped on arrival.
         */
        var CLICK_ID_PARAMS = ['gclid', 'wbraid', 'gbraid', 'fbclid', 'msclkid', 'li_fat_id', 'twclid', 'rdt_cid'];

        // Mirrors MaxAttributionValueLength on the server.
        var MAX_VALUE_LENGTH = 500;

        /*
         * The first touch travels to Cal as one JSON string, so it gets a JSON
         * bound rather than the 500-char per-value one. Truncating JSON
         * produces a string the receiver's JSON.parse rejects, which would drop
         * the whole first touch silently.
         */
        var MAX_FIRST_TOUCH_LENGTH = 4000;

        /*
         * This page's touch, kept in memory as well as written.
         *
         * Two reasons. A visitor who has not been asked yet keeps it here until
         * they answer, and it is stored the moment they accept. And a browser
         * that refuses localStorage outright (private modes, "block all site
         * data", a sandboxed iframe) swallows every write, so a reader that
         * trusted storage alone would hand Cal an empty bag for a visitor who
         * arrived on a paid click seconds earlier.
         */
        var currentTouch = null;

        function setItem(key, value) {
            try {
                window.localStorage.setItem(key, value);
            } catch (e) {
                // Storage unavailable; attribution is best-effort.
            }
        }

        function removeItem(key) {
            try {
                window.localStorage.removeItem(key);
            } catch (e) {
                // Nothing to remove from.
            }
        }

        function getItem(key) {
            try {
                return window.localStorage.getItem(key);
            } catch (e) {
                return null;
            }
        }

        function bound(value) {
            return String(value).slice(0, MAX_VALUE_LENGTH);
        }

        function isAllowed() {
            return window.oneUptimeConsent.isAllowed();
        }

        function readTouchFromUrl() {
            var urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

            var utmValues = {};
            var hasUtm = false;
            Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                var value = urlParams.get(param);
                if (value) {
                    utmValues[UTM_KEY_MAP[param]] = bound(value);
                    hasUtm = true;
                }
            });

            var clickIds = {};
            var hasClickId = false;
            CLICK_ID_PARAMS.forEach(function (param) {
                var value = urlParams.get(param);
                if (value) {
                    clickIds[param] = bound(value);
                    hasClickId = true;
                }
            });

            if (!hasUtm && !hasClickId) {
                return null;
            }

            return {
                utmValues: utmValues,
                clickIds: clickIds,
                hasClickId: hasClickId,
                url: window.location.href,
                referrer: document.referrer || '',
                timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
            };
        }

        function storeTouch(touch) {
            // New touch: clear previous last-touch values, then store this visit's.
            Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                removeItem(UTM_KEY_MAP[param]);
            });
            Object.keys(touch.utmValues).forEach(function (key) {
                setItem(key, touch.utmValues[key]);
            });
            setItem('utmUrl', touch.url);

            if (touch.hasClickId) {
                setItem('clickIds', JSON.stringify(touch.clickIds));
            } else {
                removeItem('clickIds');
            }

            // Preserve the first attributed touch forever.
            if (!getItem('firstTouch')) {
                var firstTouch = {};
                Object.keys(touch.utmValues).forEach(function (key) {
                    firstTouch[key] = touch.utmValues[key];
                });
                if (touch.hasClickId) {
                    firstTouch.clickIds = touch.clickIds;
                }
                firstTouch.landingUrl = touch.url;
                firstTouch.referrer = touch.referrer;
                firstTouch.timestamp = touch.timestamp;
                setItem('firstTouch', JSON.stringify(firstTouch));
            }
        }

        // Everything storeTouch writes, so a refusal takes all of it back.
        function clearStoredAttribution() {
            Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                removeItem(UTM_KEY_MAP[param]);
            });
            removeItem('utmUrl');
            removeItem('clickIds');
            removeItem('firstTouch');
        }

        function parseStoredJson(key) {
            var raw = getItem(key);
            if (!raw) { return null; }
            try {
                var parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
                return parsed && typeof parsed === 'object' && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : null;
            } catch (e) {
                return null;
            }
        }

        /*
         * Everything known about where this visitor came from, whether it
         * reached storage or is only in memory - and nothing at all while
         * measurement is not allowed.
         *
         * This page's touch wins: it is this page load, and the stored copy is
         * at best the same thing and at worst an older visit.
         */
        window.oneUptimeGetAttribution = function () {
            if (!isAllowed()) {
                return { utm: {}, clickIds: {}, firstTouch: null };
            }

            var utm = {};
            Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                var key = UTM_KEY_MAP[param];
                var value = (currentTouch && currentTouch.utmValues[key]) || getItem(key);
                if (value && value !== 'null' && value !== 'undefined') {
                    utm[key] = value;
                }
            });

            var utmUrl = (currentTouch && currentTouch.url) || getItem('utmUrl');
            if (utmUrl) {
                utm.utmUrl = utmUrl;
            }

            var clickIds = (currentTouch && currentTouch.hasClickId ? currentTouch.clickIds : null)
                || parseStoredJson('clickIds')
                || {};

            var firstTouch = parseStoredJson('firstTouch');

            /*
             * Storage refused the write, so there is no stored first touch to
             * read back. This visit is the only one we will ever know about,
             * which makes it the first one.
             */
            if (!firstTouch && currentTouch) {
                firstTouch = {};
                Object.keys(currentTouch.utmValues).forEach(function (key) {
                    firstTouch[key] = currentTouch.utmValues[key];
                });
                if (currentTouch.hasClickId) {
                    firstTouch.clickIds = currentTouch.clickIds;
                }
                firstTouch.landingUrl = currentTouch.url;
                firstTouch.referrer = currentTouch.referrer;
                firstTouch.timestamp = currentTouch.timestamp;
            }

            return {
                utm: utm,
                clickIds: clickIds,
                firstTouch: firstTouch
            };
        };

        /*
         * The same attribution, flattened into the scalar string map Cal.com
         * accepts as booking metadata.
         *
         * Cal takes booking metadata as FLAT, BRACKETED keys on the embed
         * config - `metadata[utm_source]` - and hands them back on the webhook
         * as payload.metadata.utm_source. NOT as a nested `metadata: {...}`
         * object: Cal serialises each config value into a query parameter, so a
         * nested object becomes the string "[object Object]" and every key
         * inside it is lost. Nothing errors; bookings keep succeeding, they
         * just arrive attributable to nothing - indistinguishable from not
         * having done this at all.
         *
         * https://cal.com/help/embedding/prefill-booking-form-embed
         *
         * Keys are the snake_case wire spelling, which is what the CRM's Cal
         * webhook receiver parses. Returns {} when there is nothing to
         * attribute and no booking kind, so a caller can spread it
         * unconditionally without sending an empty metadata bag.
         */
        window.oneUptimeCalAttributionMetadata = function (bookingKind) {
            var attribution = window.oneUptimeGetAttribution();
            var config = {};

            function put(key, value, maxLength) {
                if (value) {
                    config['metadata[' + key + ']'] =
                        String(value).slice(0, maxLength || MAX_VALUE_LENGTH);
                }
            }

            Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                put(param, attribution.utm[UTM_KEY_MAP[param]]);
            });

            put('utm_url', attribution.utm.utmUrl);

            Object.keys(attribution.clickIds).forEach(function (param) {
                put(param, attribution.clickIds[param]);
            });

            if (attribution.firstTouch) {
                var serialized = JSON.stringify(attribution.firstTouch);
                if (serialized.length <= MAX_FIRST_TOUCH_LENGTH) {
                    put('ou_first_touch', serialized, MAX_FIRST_TOUCH_LENGTH);
                }
            }

            /*
             * Unconditional, unlike everything above it, and not personal
             * data. All three embeds book the same Cal event type
             * (oneuptimehq/demo), so without this the receiver cannot tell a
             * support call from an enterprise demo from a self-hosted
             * architecture assessment - they arrive identical.
             */
            if (bookingKind) {
                config['metadata[ou_booking_kind]'] = String(bookingKind).slice(0, MAX_VALUE_LENGTH);
            }

            return config;
        };

        var touch = readTouchFromUrl();

        if (touch) {
            currentTouch = touch;
        }

        if (isAllowed()) {
            if (touch) {
                storeTouch(touch);
            }
        } else {
            // Stored on an earlier visit, before measurement was gated.
            clearStoredAttribution();
        }

        window.oneUptimeConsent.onChange(function (allowed) {
            if (allowed) {
                if (currentTouch) {
                    storeTouch(currentTouch);
                }
            } else {
                clearStoredAttribution();
            }
        });

        /*
         * Reporting is the including page's business, not this partial's.
         *
         * The marketing site emits a `home/`-prefixed PostHog event from here;
         * the product origins emit nothing, and must not start emitting under
         * a `home/` name just because they share the capture code. So the
         * touch is handed out and the page decides what, if anything, to do
         * with it - and only while measurement is allowed.
         *
         * Wire keys (utm_source), not property keys (utmSource): this is what
         * arrived on the URL.
         */
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
            if (!touch || typeof window.oneUptimeOnAttributionCaptured !== 'function') {
                return;
            }

            window.oneUptimeConsent.whenAllowed(function () {
                var eventProps = { utm_url: touch.url };
                Object.keys(UTM_KEY_MAP).forEach(function (param) {
                    if (touch.utmValues[UTM_KEY_MAP[param]]) {
                        eventProps[param] = touch.utmValues[UTM_KEY_MAP[param]];
                    }
                });
                Object.keys(touch.clickIds).forEach(function (param) {
                    eventProps[param] = touch.clickIds[param];
                });

                window.oneUptimeOnAttributionCaptured(eventProps);
            });
        });
    })();
</script>
